{"page":94,"verses":[{"verse_key":"4:95","surah":4,"ayah":95,"ar_uthmani":"لَّا يَسْتَوِى ٱلْقَـٰعِدُونَ مِنَ ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ غَيْرُ أُو۟لِى ٱلضَّرَرِ وَٱلْمُجَـٰهِدُونَ فِى سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ بِأَمْوَٰلِهِمْ وَأَنفُسِهِمْ ۚ فَضَّلَ ٱللَّهُ ٱلْمُجَـٰهِدِينَ بِأَمْوَٰلِهِمْ وَأَنفُسِهِمْ عَلَى ٱلْقَـٰعِدِينَ دَرَجَةً ۚ وَكُلًّا وَعَدَ ٱللَّهُ ٱلْحُسْنَىٰ ۚ وَفَضَّلَ ٱللَّهُ ٱلْمُجَـٰهِدِينَ عَلَى ٱلْقَـٰعِدِينَ أَجْرًا عَظِيمًا","en_translation_id":85,"en":"Those believers who stay at home, apart from those with an incapacity, are not equal to those who commit themselves and their possessions to striving in God’s way. God has raised such people to a rank above those who stay at home- although He has promised all believers a good reward, those who strive are favoured with a tremendous reward above those who stay at home-","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"لَّا","en_gloss":"Not","transliteration":"lā","verse_key":"4:95"},{"pos":2,"ar":"يَسْتَوِى","en_gloss":"(are) equal","transliteration":"yastawī","verse_key":"4:95"},{"pos":3,"ar":"ٱلْقَـٰعِدُونَ","en_gloss":"the ones who sit","transliteration":"l-qāʿidūna","verse_key":"4:95"},{"pos":4,"ar":"مِنَ","en_gloss":"among","transliteration":"mina","verse_key":"4:95"},{"pos":5,"ar":"ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ","en_gloss":"the believers","transliteration":"l-mu'minīna","verse_key":"4:95"},{"pos":6,"ar":"غَيْرُ","en_gloss":"other than","transliteration":"ghayru","verse_key":"4:95"},{"pos":7,"ar":"أُو۟لِى","en_gloss":"the ones (who are)","transliteration":"ulī","verse_key":"4:95"},{"pos":8,"ar":"ٱلضَّرَرِ","en_gloss":"[the] disabled","transliteration":"l-ḍarari","verse_key":"4:95"},{"pos":9,"ar":"وَٱلْمُجَـٰهِدُونَ","en_gloss":"and the ones who strive","transliteration":"wal-mujāhidūna","verse_key":"4:95"},{"pos":10,"ar":"فِى","en_gloss":"in","transliteration":"fī","verse_key":"4:95"},{"pos":11,"ar":"سَبِيلِ","en_gloss":"(the) way","transliteration":"sabīli","verse_key":"4:95"},{"pos":12,"ar":"ٱللَّهِ","en_gloss":"(of) Allah","transliteration":"l-lahi","